---
import Site from "../../layouts/Site.astro";
import CTA from "../../components/CTA.astro";
import EngineVisual from "../../components/EngineVisual.astro";
import AuditClose from "../../components/AuditClose.astro";
---

<Site
  page="engine"
  title="The Anchorline AI Growth Engine | Anchorline Systems"
  description="See how Anchorline connects market intelligence, demand, conversations, qualification, conversion, and measurement into one operated growth system."
>
  <section class="container page-hero hero-with-visual">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">THE ANCHORLINE AI GROWTH ENGINE</p><h1>
        Intelligence<br />into action.<br /><span class="accent-word"
          >As one system.</span>
      </h1><p class="hero-lede">
        A connected operating model for customer acquisition. Built around your
        buyers, your sales motion, and the work required to turn interest into
        opportunity.
      </p><CTA location="engine-hero" />
    </div><EngineVisual compact />
  </section>
  <section class="section engine-section">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">FROM SIGNAL TO NEXT STEP</p><h2>
        Growth is a sequence.<br />Not a service menu.
      </h2><div
        class="system-ribbon"
        role="img"
        aria-label="Signals inform intelligence, intelligence coordinates action, and action creates feedback through conversations and conversion."
      >
        <span>Market signals</span><b aria-hidden="true">→</b><span
          >Intelligence</span
        ><b aria-hidden="true">→</b><span>Coordinated action</span><b
          aria-hidden="true">→</b
        ><span>Conversations & conversion</span><div class="feedback-line mono">
          MEASURE · REVIEW · IMPROVE · REPEAT
        </div>
      </div><p class="wide-copy">
        Research, outbound, search, content, websites, paid demand, and
        automation are capabilities inside that sequence. We select them because
        they support the acquisition motion—not because a package needs more
        line items.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section container" id="outputs">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">THE OPERATING OUTPUTS</p><h2>
          Work you can see.<br />Decisions you can use.
        </h2>
      </div><p class="section-intro">
        Illustrative output categories. The engagement determines which are
        required; these are not claims of client results.
      </p>
    </div><div class="output-ledger">
      <article>
        <span class="mono">INTELLIGENCE</span><h3>Know where to focus.</h3><p>
          Market and account research, buyer context, opportunity
          prioritization, visibility observations, and decision-ready briefs.
        </p>
      </article><article>
        <span class="mono">ACQUISITION</span><h3>
          Make the approach relevant.
        </h3><p>
          Outbound acquisition plans, personalized prospect assets, search-ready
          content structures, and paid-demand readiness where appropriate.
        </p>
      </article><article>
        <span class="mono">CONVERSION</span><h3>
          Give interest somewhere to go.
        </h3><p>
          Premium websites, landing pages, lead-capture paths, conversion
          improvements, and follow-up structures.
        </p>
      </article><article>
        <span class="mono">OPERATIONS</span><h3>
          Keep the system coordinated.
        </h3><p>
          Defined responsibilities, review queues, scoped automation, operating
          reports, and analytics that support the next decision.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section orchestration-section">
    <div class="container editorial-split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">AI CAPABILITY. HUMAN ACCOUNTABILITY.</p><h2>
          Coordinated work.<br />Clear ownership.
        </h2><p>
          AI can accelerate the work. It does not remove the need for judgment,
          priorities, or accountable execution.
        </p>
      </div><div
        class="workforce-map"
        role="img"
        aria-label="Conceptual operating roles: intelligence, acquisition, and conversion work are coordinated under human oversight, with measurement feeding review."
      >
        <div class="oversight mono">
          HUMAN OVERSIGHT / GOALS · APPROVALS · REVIEW
        </div><div class="workforce-lanes">
          <div>
            <span class="role-symbol">01</span><strong>Intelligence</strong
            ><small>Research & context</small>
          </div><div>
            <span class="role-symbol">02</span><strong>Acquisition</strong
            ><small>Demand & conversations</small>
          </div><div>
            <span class="role-symbol">03</span><strong>Conversion</strong><small
              >Digital execution & capture</small>
          </div>
        </div><div class="oversight mono">
          SHARED CONTEXT → MEASUREMENT → NEXT ACTION
        </div><p class="artifact-note">
          Illustrative roles, not a live staffing or performance display.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section container editorial-split">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">SUPPORTING OPERATING INFRASTRUCTURE</p><h2>
        Built on more than<br />disconnected tools.
      </h2>
    </div><div class="editorial-copy">
      <p class="large-copy">
        2ndBrainOS is Anchorline’s proprietary operating framework for
        intelligence, automation, knowledge, and execution.
      </p><p>
        It supports the coordination behind the Growth Engine. For clients, the
        value is a more connected approach to the work—not another separate
        product to assemble or manage.
      </p><p>
        It is a supporting Anchorline capability, not a competing Growth Engine
        offer. Private implementation details and environments remain private.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section container configuration-links">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">CHOOSE YOUR ACQUISITION MOTION</p><h2>
        Same engine.<br />Different configurations.
      </h2>
    </div><div>
      <a href="/growth-engine/b2b/"
        ><span class="mono">B2B GROWTH</span><strong
          >From buyer intelligence<br />to qualified conversations.</strong
        ><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
      ><a href="/growth-engine/local/"
        ><span class="mono">LOCAL GROWTH</span><strong
          >From being found<br />to being chosen.</strong
        ><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </div>
  </section>
  <AuditClose />
</Site>
